{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"756b2d7c-ce16-49bd-aa76-08200ba79caa","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A vector shows a displacement: both its length and direction matter. Start with vector A pointing right.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Adding vectors head to tail"},{"op":"arrow","id":"vector_a","region":"right","from":[0.15,0.75],"to":[0.6,0.75],"stroke":"solid","label":"A"},{"op":"text","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Keep each length and direction."}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"756b2d7c-ce16-49bd-aa76-08200ba79caa","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Place vector B with its tail at A's head. Here B points upward. Sliding a vector does not change it.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"vector_b","canvas_id":"vector_a","from":[0.6,0.75],"to":[0.6,0.25],"stroke":"solid","label":"B"},{"op":"point","id":"join","canvas_id":"vector_a","at":[0.6,0.75]},{"op":"text","id":"head_tail","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"A's head meets B's tail."}],"checkpoint":{"question":"When moving B into place, may we rotate it?","expected_gist":"No. Its direction and length must stay unchanged."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"756b2d7c-ce16-49bd-aa76-08200ba79caa","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The sum connects the starting tail to the final head. Draw this resultant directly from the start to the finish.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"resultant","canvas_id":"vector_a","from":[0.15,0.75],"to":[0.6,0.25],"stroke":"solid","label":"R"},{"op":"equation","id":"sum","anchor":{"el":"head_tail","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\vec R=\\vec A+\\vec B"},{"op":"point","id":"start","canvas_id":"vector_a","at":[0.15,0.75],"label":"start"},{"op":"point","id":"finish","canvas_id":"vector_a","at":[0.6,0.25],"label":"finish"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"756b2d7c-ce16-49bd-aa76-08200ba79caa","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Following A then B gives the same overall displacement as R alone. The resultant points toward the finish, not back toward the start.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"conclusion","anchor":{"el":"sum","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Two moves → one net displacement."}],"checkpoint":null}}
